{# editorial treatment (A3-landscape hero, archetype "editorial").

   Reworked to render the ABOUT page (ST-05), where its rich editorial data fits:
   the 30-50% figure, the 100+ / €200k+ figures, and the partner wall. Driven
   ENTIRELY by TreatmentData (`td`).

     LEFT  cream field (~62%): a TOP / MIDDLE / BOTTOM distributed stack that
                               FILLS the full A3 height (no dead band, top OR
                               bottom):
       TOP    : eyebrow ("Über uns") + two-tone serif headline + a lede (the
                About thesis, td.body[0]).
       MIDDLE : the VISUAL HEART, a METRICS ZONE. A teal proportion DONUT (reused
                from components/viz_proportion.jinja via the viz dispatch) shows
                the PROPORTION stat verbatim (e.g. "30-50%" with its label) NEXT
                TO the other stats as big serif KPI callouts (100+ / AI-Projekte,
                €200k+ / Einsparung/Jahr). The proportion stat is the one whose
                value carries a "%"; it drives the donut and is NOT repeated as a
                KPI (one proof device per metric). When no stat carries a "%", all
                stats render as KPIs and the donut is omitted (graceful).
       BOTTOM : a CLOSING paragraph block anchored at the foot of the field. It
                renders the REMAINING body paragraphs (td.body[1:]) so the About
                thesis (the founder's closing story) closes the field at the bottom
                edge, filling the band the metrics zone left open. When the body
                has only ONE paragraph, the bottom is anchored instead by a
                compact credibility line drawn from td.list_items (graceful: when
                neither is present, the metrics zone simply absorbs the slack).

     RIGHT navy column (~38%): a full-bleed portrait from td.image (painted via a
                               CSS background, face-safe cover), a scrim caption =
                               founder name + role (td.caption), and a "Vertrauen
                               von" credential wall from td.credentials (the 3
                               partners), stacked with thin on-dark dividers.

   Reference: treatments/refs/{html,png}/treat_editorial_v2. The mockup's
   hardcoded apex strings + hex + font names are DEMO content; this template reads
   only `td` and the page-scoped CSS uses semantic tokens ONLY (styles/
   treatments/editorial.css). Every block graceful-omits when its data is absent.

   The founder portrait + name + role on the About page arrive via the
   founder-identity fallback (the assembler injects a resolved `founder` slot +
   an `author` onto the About page before rendering, since ST-05 has no portrait
   of its own); adapt() then resolves td.image + td.caption from them. #}
{% from 'eyebrow.jinja' import eyebrow %}
{% from 'two_tone_headline.jinja' import two_tone_headline %}
{% from 'viz.jinja' import viz as render_viz %}

{# ---- METRICS ZONE split: the PROPORTION stat (value carries a "%") drives the
   donut; the rest become KPI callouts. The figure is shown VERBATIM in the ring,
   so a range like "30-50%" reads exactly as authored. The arc uses a fixed,
   sensible ~40% sweep (a range has no single percent), so the ring reads as a
   proportion device without implying a precise value. ---- #}
{% set ns = namespace(donut_stat=none, kpis=[]) %}
{% for s in (td.stats or []) %}
  {% if ns.donut_stat is none and (s.value and '%' in (s.value | string)) %}
    {% set ns.donut_stat = s %}
  {% else %}
    {% set _ = ns.kpis.append(s) %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set donut_specs = [] %}
{% if ns.donut_stat %}
  {% set _ = donut_specs.append({
      'preset': 'donut',
      'figure': ns.donut_stat.value,
      'percent': 40,
      'label': ns.donut_stat.label or ''
  }) %}
{% else %}
  {# %-figures now arrive as READY donut specs on td.viz (the writer-v4
     kennzahlen/anteil routing moved them OUT of stats) - without this
     fallback the hero's proportion ring silently disappeared. #}
  {% for v in (td.viz or []) %}
    {% if not donut_specs and v.preset == 'donut' %}
      {% set _ = donut_specs.append(v) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{# the navy MARBLE panel texture (a package report asset), resolved to a file://
   URI via the context and exposed as a CSS custom property so the page-scoped CSS
   can paint it on the curved footer band + the dark portrait column WITHOUT a path
   literal in the CSS (brand-agnostic). Graceful: when absent, the CSS falls back to
   the flat var(--color-ink) ground. #}
{% set _marble = ctx.resolve_report_asset(("panel_texture",), ("panel_texture",)) %}

<div class="ed-grid"{% if _marble %} style="--panel-marble: url('{{ _marble }}');"{% endif %}>

  {# ---- the CURVED MARBLE FOOTER sweeping the page bottom (replaces the rejected
     sine wave). A full-width navy-marble band with ONE graceful curved top edge +
     a double teal hairline, painted FIRST so the absolute navy column lands on top
     of it on the right (the band + column read as one connected navy mass at the
     foot, like the reference). The marble fill is masked to the curve; the hairline
     SVG is a separate, un-clipped layer tracing the same sweep. The closing thesis
     sits ABOVE the band (the cream field reserves bottom room for it). #}
  <div class="ed-footer" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="ed-footer-fill"></div>
    <svg class="ed-footer-edge" viewBox="0 0 1200 200" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <path class="ed-edge-lo" d="M0 107 C 175 43 345 27 515 37 C 770 52 985 73 1200 81" fill="none"/>
      <path class="ed-edge-hi" d="M0 104 C 175 40 345 24 515 34 C 770 49 985 70 1200 78" fill="none"/>
    </svg>
  </div>

  {# ---- LEFT: the cream editorial field (distributed stack) ---- #}
  <div class="ed-field">

    {# TOP: eyebrow + headline + lede #}
    <div class="ed-field-head">
      {% if td.eyebrow %}{{ eyebrow(td.eyebrow) }}{% endif %}
      {% if td.headline %}
        {{ two_tone_headline(td.headline, td.headline_accent or '', tag='h1') }}
      {% endif %}
      {% if td.body and td.body[0] %}<p class="ed-lede">{{ td.body[0] }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>

    {# MIDDLE: the metrics zone -- the donut + KPI callouts (the visual heart).
       Rendered only when there is a donut OR at least one KPI. #}
    {% if donut_specs or ns.kpis %}
    <div class="ed-field-mid">
      <div class="ed-metrics-cap">In Zahlen</div>
      <div class="ed-metrics">
        {% if donut_specs %}
        <div class="ed-donut" aria-label="Proportionsdiagramm">
          {{ render_viz(donut_specs) }}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if ns.kpis %}
        <div class="ed-kpis">
          {% for s in ns.kpis %}
          <div class="ed-kpi">
            {% if s.value %}<span class="ed-kpi-value">{{ s.value }}</span>{% endif %}
            {% if s.label %}<span class="ed-kpi-label">{{ s.label }}</span>{% endif %}
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# BOTTOM: the closing block, anchored at the FOOT of the cream field so the
       left column fills top-to-bottom. Prefers the remaining body paragraphs
       (td.body[1:], the founding thesis); when the body is a single paragraph it
       falls back to a compact credibility line from td.list_items. Graceful: when
       neither is present nothing renders and the metrics zone absorbs the slack. #}
    {% set closing = td.body[1:] if (td.body and td.body | length > 1) else [] %}
    {% if closing %}
    <div class="ed-field-foot">
      <span class="ed-foot-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {% for para in closing %}<p class="ed-foot-para">{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% elif td.list_items %}
    <div class="ed-field-foot">
      <span class="ed-foot-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <ul class="ed-foot-points">
        {% for item in td.list_items %}<li class="ed-foot-point">{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

  </div>

  {# ---- RIGHT: the dark portrait column (founder identity) ---- #}
  <div class="ed-column">
    {% if td.image %}
    <div class="ed-portrait" style="background-image:url('{{ td.image }}');">
      {% if td.caption and (td.caption.name or td.caption.role) %}
      <figcaption class="ed-caption">
        {% if td.caption.name %}<span class="ed-caption-name">{{ td.caption.name }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if td.caption.role %}<span class="ed-caption-role">{{ td.caption.role }}</span>{% endif %}
      </figcaption>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if td.credentials %}
    <div class="ed-creds">
      {{ eyebrow('Vertrauen von') }}
      <ul class="ed-creds-list">
        {% for name in td.credentials %}
        <li class="ed-creds-item">{{ name }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

</div>
